{"content":[{"c":["DIVORCE*, Certificate of"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["A document declaring the separation of a husband and wife, mandated by Mosaic law (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.24.1-4","r":"Deut.24.1-4","rawR":"Deut.24.1-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.24.1-4","value":"Deut.24.1-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 24:1-4"},"; see ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.5.31","r":"Matt.5.31","rawR":"Matt.5.31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.5.31","value":"Matt.5.31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 5:31"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.19.7","r":"Matt.19.7","rawR":"Matt.19.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.19.7","value":"Matt.19.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"19:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Mark.10.4","r":"Mark.10.4","rawR":"Mark.10.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.10.4","value":"Mark.10.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 10:4"},"). The certificate of divorce protected the woman’s rights, providing evidence of her freedom and ensuring that her husband could not claim her dowry. An example of the wording of such a document is ",{"href":"?bref=Hos.2.2","r":"Hos.2.2","rawR":"Hos.2.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Hos.2.2","value":"Hos.2.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Hosea 2:2"},": “She is no longer my wife, and I am no longer her husband” (",{"c":["nlt"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"). The OT prophets used this statement figuratively to portray God’s desire to separate himself from his rebellious people (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.50.1","r":"Isa.50.1","rawR":"Isa.50.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.50.1","value":"Isa.50.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 50:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.3.8","r":"Jer.3.8","rawR":"Jer.3.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.3.8","value":"Jer.3.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 3:8"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=CivilLawandJustice_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"CivilLawandJustice_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"CivilLawandJustice_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Civil Law and Justice"},"; ",{"href":"?item=Divorce_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Divorce_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Divorce_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Divorce"},"; ",{"href":"?item=MarriageMarriageCustoms_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"MarriageMarriageCustoms_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"MarriageMarriageCustoms_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Marriage, Marriage Customs"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"DivorceCertificateof","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Dt 24:1-4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.24.1-4","rawQueryValue":"Deut.24.1-4","sourceRefExact":"Deut.24.1-4"},{"anchorText":"Mt 5:31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.5.31","rawQueryValue":"Matt.5.31","sourceRefExact":"Matt.5.31"},{"anchorText":"19:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.19.7","rawQueryValue":"Matt.19.7","sourceRefExact":"Matt.19.7"},{"anchorText":"Mk 10:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mark.10.4","rawQueryValue":"Mark.10.4","sourceRefExact":"Mark.10.4"},{"anchorText":"Hosea 2:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Hos.2.2","rawQueryValue":"Hos.2.2","sourceRefExact":"Hos.2.2"},{"anchorText":"Is 50:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.50.1","rawQueryValue":"Isa.50.1","sourceRefExact":"Isa.50.1"},{"anchorText":"Jer 3:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.3.8","rawQueryValue":"Jer.3.8","sourceRefExact":"Jer.3.8"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"b35447aa6f6a0091cb5a009e055870ab5fcbd096142bd0be732a21c5d9c838e7","sourceItemName":"DivorceCertificateof","sourceItemOrder":140,"sourc